WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:07.030
Hi, I'm Thinh Tran, a Computer Science co-op student at York University's Lassonde School of Engineering,

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:08.140
graduating in 2028.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.348
I'm looking for my next co-op term in Summer 2027,

00:00:11.348 --> 00:00:14.380
in software engineering, and here's why I do what I do.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.422
When I was eight, I met a friend in elementary school,

00:00:17.422 --> 00:00:19.540
and fifteen years later we're still friends.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.040
His parents were immigrants without much, and he struggled in school.

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.920
Then, at university, he dove deep into his studies and worked every day,

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.080
building random projects just to get noticed.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.771
With no connections,

00:00:30.771 --> 00:00:34.940
he's now a senior software engineer at one of Canada's biggest banks.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.197
I started university in nursing, but he knew I loved creating and exploring,

00:00:39.197 --> 00:00:42.360
and his perseverance inspired me to switch to computer science.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.168
Today, as an intern at Groupe Bel Canada, I train teams to use AI tools,

00:00:47.168 --> 00:00:49.860
and that work brought me to Paris this week.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.820
I also built the online ordering site for my family's Vietnamese restaurant,

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.280
which serves real customers, and a resume pipeline that's public on GitHub.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.283
My goal is to become a software engineer who keeps building and keeps learning,

00:01:02.283 --> 00:01:03.480
just like my friend.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.600
My ePortfolio and LinkedIn are linked below.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.997
Connect with me,

00:01:07.997 --> 00:01:12.480
and I'll reach out to book a 15-minute chat about your Summer 2027 co-op roles.
